  "worked_solution": "Starting from the equation $r\\cdot s=1,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $z$ and then solve for $z$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & =1 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot (z+1)+z\\cdot (-9)+4\\cdot z+1\\cdot 7 & =1 \\\\ -6+6z+6-9z+4z+7 & =1 \\\\ z & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $z=-6.$",
